Problem Statement: Course Management System  Mock3

Objective:

Develop a console-based C# application using ADO.NET to perform CRU (Create, Read, Update) operations on a Course table in a SQL Server database. The application should enable users to add new courses, display course details by ID, show courses with prices above 1000, and update course prices. The project should be implemented using a disconnected architecture with SqlConnection, SqlDataAdapter and SqlCommandBuilder and all classes, properties, and methods should be made public."







Classes and Properties:

Course Class (in Models folder):

The Course class represents a course entity with the following public properties:
CourseID (int): Unique identifier for each course. Auto-incremented in the database.
CourseName (string): The name of the course.
Price (decimal): The price of the course.
Instructor (string): The name of the course instructor.


Methods:

AddCourse(Course course):

Inserts a new course into the Course table in the database.

Parameters: A Course object containing the details of the course to be added.
Displays the added course's details after successful insertion.
Console Messages:
"Course added successfully."


DisplayCourseById(int courseID):

Retrieves and displays the details of a course from the Course table using its CourseID.

Parameters: The CourseID of the course to display.
Console Messages:
If the course is found: The details of the course are printed as below.
CourseID: {row["CourseID"]}\tCourseName: {row["CourseName"]}\tPrice: {row["Price"]}\tInstructor: {row["Instructor"]}
If no course is found: "No course found with ID {courseID}."


DisplayCoursesWithPriceAbove1000():

Retrieves and displays all courses with a price above 1000 from the Course table.
Console Messages:
If courses are found: The details of each course are printed as below:
CourseID: {row["CourseID"]}\tCourseName: {row["CourseName"]}\tPrice: {row["Price"]}\tInstructor: {row["Instructor"]}
If no courses are found: "No courses with price above 1000 found."


UpdateCourse(int courseID, decimal newPrice):

Updates the price of an existing course based on the provided CourseID.

Parameters: The CourseID and the new price value.
Console Messages:
If the course is successfully updated: "Course price updated successfully."
The details of the book are printed as below:
CourseID: {row["CourseID"]}\tCourseName: {row["CourseName"]}\tPrice: {row["Price"]}\tInstructor: {row["Instructor"]}
If no course is found: "No course found with ID {courseID}."


Program Class:

The Program class serves as the entry point for the Course Management System. It interacts with the user input and oversee the application flow.

Main function: (Prompt all the user inputs in the Main function itself):
Prompts the user to input course details such as course name, price and instructor.
Menu options:
The main menu serves as the user interface for interacting with the system. It provides the following options:
Course Management Menu
Add Course
Display Course by ID
Display Courses with Price Above 1000
Update Course
Exit - Terminates the application with the message "Exiting program...".
Invalid choice: Displays "Invalid choice, please try again."


Database Details:

Database Name: appdb

Table Name: Course

Ensure that the database connection is properly established using the ConnectionStringProvider class.



Note:

Do not change the class names. 

Do not change the skeleton (Structure of the project given)



Commands to Run the Project:

cd dotnetapp - Select the dotnet project folder
dotnet restore - This command will restore all the required packages to run the application.
dotnet run - To run the application in port 8080 (The settings preloaded click 8080 Port to View)
dotnet build - To build and check for errors
dotnet clean - If the same error persists clean the project and build again
dotnet add package package_name --version 6.0 - Any package if required you can install by the above command. The package that you are installing should support the .Net 6.0 version.


To Work with SQLServer:

(Open a New Terminal) type the below commands

sqlcmd -U sa 

password: examlyMssql@123

 

>use DBName

>go
